  "body": "# Tibicen 1.5.2\n\nFixes initial setup after installing Tibicen inside a project. The canonical `tibicen-init` and `tibicen-adopt` folders alone no longer count as an existing user setup. Other instructions, skills, registered memory and recorded setup still select improvement. User rule/command/MCP directories retain ownership of nested example paths.\n\nComplete inventory, file modes, nonempty-project protection, exact approval and application-write boundaries are unchanged. No migration, schema or dependency change is needed. Folder-name recognition is a routing hint, not proof of trust or provenance.\n\nValidation: 1,048 passing tests and one existing skip; three standalone checks; all six macOS/Linux/Windows and Node 22/24 cells; exact local/public installation, replacement, repeated add, edited-backup restoration and removal. One fresh subscription Codex cycle completed proposal, approved apply, a useful task with five independent tests, and a read-only repeat without changes. This does not establish measured human benefit or compatibility with every harness/model. Another proposal lacked its compiled envelope in the retained native output and was not applied; the evidence gap remains recorded.\n\nInstall the exact distribution:\n\n```sh\nnpx skills@1.7.4 add https://github.com/warbr1ng3r/tibicen/tree/df15ae7e0ae67aee2bd278f7e4f265e03437e672 -g --agent universal --skill tibicen-init tibicen-adopt --copy\n```\n\n[Source](https://github.com/warbr1ng3r/tibicen/commit/f5bc0a416813c54d3ec21e50f3f5ede0b4be2bb8) · [CI](https://github.com/warbr1ng3r/tibicen/actions/runs/42424557875) · [Six platforms](https://github.com/warbr1ng3r/tibicen/actions/runs/42424565552) · [Release checks and limits](https://github.com/warbr1ng3r/tibicen/blob/main/docs/evals/results/2026-11-08-release-1.5.2/README.md)\n"
